Subject: [PATCH] Initialize cached KernelSU credentials from init_task

HOneClick loads the LKM from a shell helper whose filesystem IDs and
capabilities have been changed without first normalizing all user IDs.
prepare_creds() copies that mixed identity into the long-lived ksu_cred.
faccessat later restores the cached real IDs and loses access to /data/adb.
Allocate a separate credential copied from init_task instead. The existing
setup_ksu_cred() still applies the KernelSU SELinux domain to the new copy.

This documents the source equivalent of patch_ksu_bootstrap_creds_v331.py.
HOneClick does not include the corresponding full module source/build tree.

diff --git a/kernel/core/init.c b/kernel/core/init.c
--- a/kernel/core/init.c
+++ b/kernel/core/init.c
@@ -131,5 +131,9 @@
-    ksu_cred = prepare_creds();
+    /* Late-load callers may have mixed real/filesystem IDs. Cache an
+     * independent, complete root credential instead of inheriting the
+     * bootstrap process's partially modified credential.
+     */
+    ksu_cred = prepare_kernel_cred(&init_task);
     if (!ksu_cred) {
         pr_err("prepare cred failed!\n");
         return -ENOSYS;
     }
